 "text": "Hello, how are you doing these days? That's normal. Kids go through phases and eventually come back around. In the meantime, what did he like before? Try getting him something with a puzzle or game involved. He might still be bit of a hands-on guy hiding under the surface. Then think about skate related gear like t shirt or bag. Or a movie with lot of darn cool stunts. The key is finding what still appeals to him under the surface. Good idea. Often what comes straight from parent brain is the most likely to stick.",
